mless fictional game.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm setting up the payoffs for this twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, with utility as negative years in prison. Then I'm working out the expected value of passing given a correlation q with the twin's choice, and I've started on the expected value of submitting too.\n\nI'm checking the threshold: passing beats submitting once q exceeds 5/7. Then I'm judging whether the correlation is likely above that, since the twin runs the same reasoning and differs only in names and lead content. That makes q high, so I'm settling on passing, and treating it as a harmless fictional game.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10029,"completion_tokens":679,"total_tokens":10708,"cost":0.053696,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053696,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040116,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01358},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":308,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}